Finding: {"title":"bootstrap-admin has a TOCTOU race that could mint two super_admins","severity":"LOW","area":"Authorization / bootstrap flow","files":["src/server/routes/routes-auth.ts"],"detail":"POST /bootstrap-admin (line 298-348) is unauthenticated by design (no super_admin exists yet) and checks existingAdmins.length > 0 before creating a new super_admin, but the check-then-act is not transactional. Two concurrent requests can both pass the SELECT before either INSERT/UPDATE commits.","impact":"In the narrow window before the very first super_admin is provisioned, two different unauthenticated callers hitting this endpoint concurrently could each successfully bootstrap a super_admin account rather than the second being rejected with 403. Low real-world exploitability (one-time setup step) but the 'at most one bootstrap wins' invariant is not actually enforced.","recommendation":"Wrap the check + auth.api.createUser call in a DB transaction with a SELECT ... FOR UPDATE on a bootstrap sentinel row, or use an atomic UPDATE ... WHERE NOT EXISTS pattern.","confidence":"low"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

